# White-label Branding (Permanent)

## Law

**Three brand layers — never conflate:**

| Layer | Store | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| App chrome dark/light | Cookie `vdb-theme` | Product UI only |
| Document brand | `design_themes` | PDF / editor document tokens |
| **White-label** | `business_branding` | Customer logo, shell name/colors, hide Powered-by, custom domain |

## Capability (Edition × entitlement)

| Capability | `SELF_HOSTED` | `SAAS` without `branding.white_label` | `SAAS` with entitlement |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Edit branding (name, colors, logo) | ✓ | ✗ (upgrade CTA) | ✓ |
| Hide “Powered by” | ✓ (default on) | ✗ | ✓ |
| Custom domain (DNS → install) | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ |

Canonical entitlement: `branding.white_label` (`EntitlementCodes.BrandingWhiteLabel`) — SAAS paid add-on; **SELF_HOSTED treats as always allowed** (no catalog purchase required).

## Data model

Table `business_branding` (1:1 `business_id`):

- `display_name`, `primary_color` (hex), `logo_storage_key` / mime / size
- `custom_domain` (hostname, unique when set), `hide_powered_by`
- Soft-delete not required; row upserted on first save

Logo storage key:

```text
{businessId}/branding/logo.{png|jpg|webp|svg-forbidden}
```

Same `STORAGE_DRIVER` as media — never Mongo for bytes. SVG upload forbidden (XSS).

## API / gates

- `GET .../branding` — membership (includes `capabilities` flags)
- `PATCH .../branding`, logo upload/delete — `EntitlementGuard` + writable + `@RequirePermission(manage.settings)` + white-label capability assert
- `GET .../branding/logo/file` — membership
- `GET /api/branding/resolve?host=` — public (for future Web Publish / custom domain)

## UI

- Settings page `/app/branding`
- App shell consumes branding: display name, accent, logo, footer Powered-by when `showPoweredByEffective`
- Web Publish must reuse the same `business_branding` resolve — do not invent a second brand store (see `19-web-publish.mdc`)

## Custom domain

Document DNS in `docs/deploy/` (CNAME/A → reverse proxy, TLS). App stores hostname only; TLS/proxy is ops — API validates hostname shape and uniqueness.
